   "notes": "No article drawing; every pin from the GI AY-5-2376 datasheet. Pin functions: 1 VCC +5V (substrate); 17 VGI = GND; 18 VGG = -12V (+/-1V); 2/3/40 frequency control B/C/A (datasheet: C2 between 40 and 3, R2 between 2 and 3; R2=100k, C2=30p gives 50kHz); 4 Shift input; 5 Control input (CTRL not required -> GND); 6 Parity invert (GND); 7 Parity out (unused); 8 B8 (unused, only 7 bits needed); 9..15 = B7..B1 -> KBD_D6..KBD_D0; 16 Strobe out; 19 Strobe control (delay RC, datasheet R1=680k and C1 both to VCC); 20 Data & Strobe invert: tied to +5V so B1-B8 AND the strobe are inverted -> inverted data, active-low strobe (KBD_STROBE_N), which IC55a turns positive. 32..39 = X7..X0 (drive outputs, switch pin 1); 21..31 = Y10..Y0 (sense inputs with internal load to VGG, switch pin 2). Pin 20 tie, pin 5/6 ties, and use of -12V are inference (standard datasheet application); kit wiring unknown."
  },
