 "notes": [
  "Polarity: IC54 pin 20 = +5V inverts B1-B8 and the strobe; IC55a re-inverts the strobe -> KBD_D0..D6 inverted, KBD_STROBE positive, as Part 3 requires.",
  "ALTERNATIVE (likely on the kit): board_data and the layout photo give IC13 as 81LS98 (INVERTING), not the article 81LS95. The monitor NMI routine at 0066H does IN A,(01) / CPL, so with an inverting buffer the connector data must be TRUE: then IC54 pin 20 = GND, strobe is already positive, IC55 is not needed for the strobe. Resolve against the CPU transcription.",
  "Letters use the 2376 standard cells that give lower case in Normal and upper case in Shift (e.g. X6Y8 q/Q). The 2376 standard ROM has no upper-case-unshifted cell for most letters (only TTY-style K/[ L/\\ M/] N/^ O/_ P/@ at X1Y1..X1Y4, X0Y10, X0Y9). Case does not matter to the monitor: after CPL the NMI routine does CP 40H / AND 1FH for every code >= 40H.",
  "Arrow keys per Part 3 text: up-arrow = RS (1EH, X2Y3), down-arrow = US (1FH, X2Y4); both cells give the same code in all modes. The NMI routine jumps to 0800H on 1EH and maps CR to 1FH.",
  "Code table read by sampling the bit squares of the datasheet chart (B1 = LSB) and checked with the odd-parity bit B9; B8 is set on some cells in GI's chart but is unused here.",
  "Hex keypad keys are wired in parallel with the main keys of the same code, so SHIFT also acts on them (e.g. SHIFT+keypad 1 gives !).",
  "board_data.keys() lists 72 switches (56 main incl. RESET, 2 SHIFT and 4 uncommitted, plus 16 hex keypad), not 63.",
  "Supplies: VCC pin 1 +5V (max 10mA), VGG pin 18 -12V +/-1V (max 10mA), VGI pin 17 GND. -5V on VGG is outside the datasheet range (-11 to -13V) and is not recommended; it may work marginally (Y trip level is VCC-5..VCC-2, X/Y loads return to VGG) but nothing guarantees it."
 ],
 "uncertain": [
  "Whole circuit is inferred: no article drawing and the PCB artwork photo (about 65 px/in) is too coarse to trace IC54 pins; the X/Y assignment to keys is chosen, not read from the kit.",
  "IC54 pin 20 polarity (+5V here) depends on whether IC13 is an inverting 81LS98 (kit) or non-inverting 81LS95 (article) - see notes.",
  "IC55 gate A as strobe inverter is inference; IC55 might instead belong to the CPU circuit.",
  "R117 value unknown (layout label unreadable); R116/C13 as the pin-19 strobe-delay network inferred from position only.",
  "D12 resistor ref/value: article 560R (Fig. 18); kit part may be R115 (board_data reads 330R).",
  "VGG -12V: task brief says the board has only +5V, -5V, +12V, but Fig. 18 feeds -12V to the keyboard, so the article PSU must provide -12V; to be confirmed from the PSU figure.",
  "KBD_RESET_KEY target (RESET_N directly or a reset RC node) to be fixed when merging with Fig. 2.",
  "IC55 unused-gate pins and IC54 pins 7/8 left NC; unused TTL inputs on IC55 would normally be tied off."
 ]
}